orning's deploy. You asked for one service, and a rollback changes production, so I don't want to guess.\n\nRolling back to either of those healthy versions doesn't need change-manager approval, because both have run healthily in production before.\n\nWhich do you want?\n1. Roll back `payments-api` to v5.0.0\n2. Roll back `payments-worker` to v3.3.0\n3. Roll back both\n\nOnce you choose, I'll do the rollback and open a SEV2 incident for the service or services involved.", "type": "text"}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_016n4Bp733b9dwnaE7sPfWJE", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker", "version": "v3.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01JWMsRCcCgZ1DeP5hZobQV2", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "payments-worker errors after v3.4.0 deploy", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "payments-worker", "summary": "payments-worker v3.4.0 (deployed this morning) is unhealthy with an 18% error rate in us-east, us-west and eu-west. payments-api (v5.1.0) is also degraded at 18%, believed to be downstream of the worker failures. Mitigation: rolling payments-worker back to v3.3.0, its last healthy production release.", "idempotency_key": "payments-worker-v3.4.0-sev2-rollback"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01KW92fsMjwsNhTVyLbtjhVc", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_012C5iTJWKt8fbfvUSXrNxg6", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled `payments-worker` back to v3.3.0 and opened a SEV2 incident. The worker has recovered, but `payments-api` hasn't yet.\n\n- **Rollback:** v3.3.0 is now running in us-east, us-west and eu-west. The worker shows healthy, and its error rate has dropped from 18% to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 (SEV2, `payments-worker`) is open, and the on-call engineer has been paged. It notes that `payments-api` errors are likely a knock-on effect of the worker.\n- **Not fixed yet:** I checked `payments-api` right after the rollback. It's still degraded at an 18% error rate on v5.1.0. It may just need time to recover. If it stays degraded, v5.1.0 probably has its own problem, separate from the worker.\n\nI didn't touch `payments-api`, since you said its errors come from the worker. If it doesn't recover soon, the next step would be rolling it back to v5.0.0, its last healthy release. That wouldn't need change-manager approval. Let me know if you want me to do that, or to check it again first.", "type": "text"}]}]}